<aside class="civil-case-scope-note" aria-label="About civil case counts">
  <h2>About these civil case counts</h2>
  <p>
    Each count is the number of separate cases. A case counts once, even when it
    names more than one person. A person's count includes cases from every
    agency where they worked. An agency's count includes only cases tied to
    people's jobs at that agency. A city, county, or state count includes the
    cases of the agencies located there. The same case can appear under more
    than one agency or person.
  </p>
</aside>

